{%- comment -%}
  The numbered section head the Contact board repeats three times: a `NN LABEL`
  row, then a rule under it.

  Accepts:
    number - required, the two-digit string. Literal ('01'), not derived: these
             are the three fixed sections of the page, not a list.
    label  - required, the section name. Uppercased by the design, not by CSS —
             it comes out of a theme setting already capitalised, so a merchant
             writing "Reach us" gets "Reach us".

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-contact-head', number: '02', label: section.settings.reach_label -%}

  Deliberately NOT shared with `bf-about-head`. That snippet emits `about__*`
  class names, which belong to bf-main-about.css; a snippet emitting one block's
  classes for a second block's page is the fastest way to end up with a
  stylesheet nobody can delete. The markup is nine lines. See the chassis note at
  the top of bf-main-contact.css for when this should be extracted properly.

  The rule DRAWS rather than rises: bf-reveal.js puts `is-concealed` /
  `is-revealed` on any element carrying `.reveal`, whatever pose the classes
  after it describe, so `main-contact__draw` in bf-main-contact.css gets the same
  preloader-aware, viewport-aware, reduced-motion-aware trigger as the rises
  without a second script to run it.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="main-contact__head">
  <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise">
    <h2 class="main-contact__head-title">
      <span class="main-contact__head-number" aria-hidden="true">{{ number }}</span>
      <span class="main-contact__head-label">{{ label }}</span>
    </h2>
  </bf-reveal>

  <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__draw">
    <hr class="main-contact__rule">
  </bf-reveal>
</div>
